{
  "dom_id": "step-q32535",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.05.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(-1) & \u2248\\frac{g(-1+0.05)-g(-1-0.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(-0.95)-g(-1.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6-3.4}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.8}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18}{1} \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
